index 0000000..5ec5b72
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A successful `get` counts as "use" per the
+   docstring, but it never called `move_to_end`, so a recently-read key could
+   still be evicted as least-recently-used. Fixed by moving the key to the end
+   of the `OrderedDict` on a hit (`test_get_refreshes_recency`).
+
+2. **`put` evicted an entry even when updating an existing key.** The
+   capacity check ran unconditionally, so re-`put`ing a key in a full cache
+   evicted the LRU entry (possibly an unrelated key) before overwriting the
+   value in place. Fixed by only evicting when the key is not already present
+   (`test_updating_existing_key_does_not_evict_others`).
